<title>HUNGARY: Cofinec reports lower H1 profits.</title>
<headline>Cofinec reports lower H1 profits.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>					   Jan-June 1996   Jan-June 1995</p>
<p>Group operating profit before</p>
<p>		   interest		 21.8	vs    34.1</p>
<p>    Group net profit		     2.1	vs    10.3</p>
<p>    Net sales			    336.5	vs   327.5</p>
<p>    Costs of sales		     259.0	vs   222.9</p>
<p>    Operating costs		     51.0	vs    64.5</p>
<p>    Net other income		     4.1 loss vs     4.2 loss</p>
<p>    One-off items			  0.5 loss vs     1.8 loss</p>
<p>    Net interest income		 15.7 loss vs    14.6 loss</p>
<p>    Tax payable			    1.1	vs     0.6</p>
<p>    Minorities			     2.9	vs     8.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Cofinec S.A. is a France-registered printed packaging company which operates in Hungary, Czech Republic and Poland. Its Global Depositary Receipts are listed on the Budapest Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The figures are consolidated and they are calculated according to International Accounting Standards.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
